-- title:
--   Every point of the upper half-plane is SL₂(ℤ)-equivalent to a point of the fundamental domain
-- statement:
--   **Every point of the upper half-plane is equivalent to a point of the fundamental domain.** Let $\mathcal D=\{z:|z|\ge1,\ |\operatorname{Re}z|\le\tfrac12\}$ be the standard fundamental domain of the modular group. For every $z$ in the upper half-plane there is $g\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $g\cdot z\in\mathcal D$.
--
--   This is the existence half of the statement that $\mathcal D$ is a fundamental domain for $SL_2(\mathbb Z)$. It is used to show that $SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ is generated by $S=\begin{pmatrix}0&-1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$ and $T=\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, to describe the moduli space of elliptic curves over $\mathbb C$, and in Gauss's reduction theory of binary quadratic forms. The proof chooses $g$ maximizing $\operatorname{Im}(g\cdot z)$ and then translates.
--
--   **Formalization note.** Mathlib's `ModularGroup.exists_smul_mem_fd`. `ModularGroup.fd` is the closed set $\mathcal D$, and $SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ acts on `UpperHalfPlane` by Möbius transformations.
-- source:
--   Listed in Mathlib's curated theorem manifests (docs/1000.yaml); formalized in Mathlib as `ModularGroup.exists_smul_mem_fd`. Proof here reduces to that Mathlib result.

